# Scenario: SMT process-engineering team investigates solder bridging on a fine-pitch line.
fishbone "SMT solder-bridge defect analysis"

effect "Solder bridging on SMT line 3 at 1,850 DPPM"

category man "Man"
category machine "Machine"
category material "Material"
category method "Method"
category measurement "Measurement"
category environment "Mother Nature"

man: "Night shift trained on old recipe"
man: "Stencil wipe skipped when late"
  - "Cycle-time target rewards output"
man: "Squeegee pressure changed mid-run"
  - "Pressure set by feel, not spec"
  - "Never logged on the setup sheet"

machine: "Printer camera misaligns the board"
machine: "Reflow zone 4 runs hot"
  - "Peak 8 degrees above profile"
machine: "Stencil apertures worn on U12"
  - "Stencil past 40,000-print life"
  - "No aperture check at changeover"

material: "Paste tub past its open life"
material: "PCB pad finish varies between lots"
  - "Second supplier released untried"
material: "Type-3 paste replaced type-4"
  - "Coarser powder bridges fine pitch"

method: "Snap-off gap set from memory"
method: "Reflow profile never re-validated"
  - "No owner after the handover"
method: "Print speed raised for takt time"
  - "Separation speed left unchanged"
  - "No print study after the change"

measurement: "AOI threshold masks small bridges"
measurement: "Bridges not trended by feeder"
  - "All defects share one code"
measurement: "SPI window wider than paste spec"
  - "Window opened to cut false calls"

environment: "Paste fridge sits two rooms away"
environment: "Dock draught chills the printer"
  - "Dock door open through unload"
environment: "Line humidity above 60 percent RH"
  - "Dehumidifier down since June"
